      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(z-1)^{2}={x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $O$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand an elliptic cone centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(z-{z}_{0})^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}},\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is an elliptic cone with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(1,0,2),\\,a=c=1,\\,b=2.\n$$",
